-- A DECLAREd enum in another section may share its name with a type L4 lifted
-- out of a field. It is an ordinary declared type, so the schemas publish it as
-- one: under its name in the module schema's $defs, and with its x-l4-type in
-- the function schema (review round 1; the schema writers once recognised a
-- lifted type by its name, and treated this one as lifted too).

§ `Plots`

DECLARE Plot HAS
    `tenure` IS ONE OF Owner, Tenant

§ `Lots`

DECLARE `Plot's tenure` IS ONE OF Freehold, Leasehold

DECLARE Lot HAS
    `kind` IS A `Plot's tenure`

@export Whether a lot is freehold.
GIVEN l IS A Lot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`freehold` l MEANS l's kind EQUALS Freehold

#ASSERT `freehold` (Lot WITH kind IS Freehold)
